{
  "name": "How Long Does Custom Molding Really Take?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Ever wonder about the timeline for a custom molding project? It's a common question, and honestly, it varies. Typically, for a new injection-molded project, you're looking at an average of 8–10 weeks from start to finish. This timeframe includes everything from the initial design review to sampling and validation before moving into full production. Factors like the complexity of your part, material choice, and how quickly decisions are made can all impact the turnaround. It's not just about building the mold; it's about making sure it's perfect for your needs, so quality checks are crucial. You'll also want to consider tool life and warranty expectations, as these are tied to how long you plan to produce the product and future volume needs. Don't rush through the planning stages; taking your time here can prevent costly rework later. If you have a strict deadline or a really intricate design, talking to an experienced molder early on can help you set realistic expectations and plan accordingly. They can advise on the best approach to meet your project's demands.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
